export default {"html":"<p data-line=\"0\" class=\"code-line\">I ran into a bit of trouble, so this is a memo. I am writing it down for anyone who hits the same issue. I think it is an Ionic/Angular problem, but it might be another library—I have not narrowed it down.</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-container\"><pre class=\"shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#151e2c;color:#e1e4e8\"><code class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"2\"><span class=\"line\"><span>@angular/core@11.0.2</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>@ionic/angular@5.4.1</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span></code></pre></div><hr data-line=\"8\" class=\"code-line\">\n<p data-line=\"10\" class=\"code-line\">The latest iOS was fine, but I got a report that the site would not load on iOS 12. When I checked, I saw this error:</p>\n<blockquote data-line=\"12\" class=\"code-line\">\n<p data-line=\"12\" class=\"code-line\">ReferenceError: Can't find variable: globalThis</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p data-line=\"14\" class=\"code-line\">It had worked before, so I think a recent version upgrade caused it. Since it says globalThis is missing, I fixed it by adding it to <code>polyfills.ts</code>.</p>\n<p data-line=\"16\" class=\"code-line\">First, install <code>@ungap/global-this</code> in the terminal.</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-container\"><pre class=\"shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#151e2c;color:#e1e4e8\"><code class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"18\"><span class=\"line\"><span>npm i @ungap/global-this</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span></code></pre></div><p data-line=\"23\" class=\"code-line\">Then import it in <code>src/polyfills.ts</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-block-container\"><pre class=\"shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#151e2c;color:#e1e4e8\"><code class=\"code-line\" data-line=\"25\"><span class=\"line\"><span>/***************************************************************************************************</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span> * APPLICATION IMPORTS</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span> */</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>import '@ungap/global-this';</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span></span></span></code></pre></div><p data-line=\"33\" class=\"code-line\">Simple, right? I learned something new this time: more users than I expected have not updated their iOS version, so you need to watch out. Because they can only update on Wi‑Fi, users without Wi‑Fi at home seem to miss updates.</p>\n<p data-line=\"35\" class=\"code-line\">See you next time.</p>\n","headings":[]} as const;
